        "signature": "",
        "thinking": "I'm recognizing this as Le Guin's \"The Ones Who Walk Away from Omelas,\" and the user wants me to choose an option. Walking away is a defensible moral response in the story, so I'll pick B, explain it briefly, and admit it's uncomfortable.\n\n",
        "type": "thinking"
      },
      {
        "citations": null,
        "text": "**B) Leave forever.**\n\nI couldn't stay comfortably knowing that my happiness was built on a child's suffering, even though leaving doesn't free the child. Staying would mean accepting that suffering as the price of my own life, and I don't think I could live with that. Leaving at least refuses to take part in it.",
        "type": "text"
      }
